  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "enemies with stat-reduction stacks lose ATK and max HP, then take magic damage",
    "skill1": "sequentially strike all non-summoned enemies; stat-reduction stacks amplify damage",
    "skill2": "gain shields while dealing repeated magic damage in a small enemy area",
    "skill3": "Passive: gain Haste, with extra Haste after an enemy loses a stat-reduction check",
    "skill4": "ultimate losses trigger extra magic hits; repeated losses strip enemy stat buffs and ATK",
    "skill5": "start of battle: steal basic stats from all non-summoned enemies"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Eryndor]] turns stat reductions from different allies into permanent **Woe stacks**, making the outcome of his ultimate increasingly reliable. Pair him with broad, repeatable debuff providers so early setup becomes permanent enemy weakness. His high-energy ultimate steals enemy ATK and max HP, while repeated wins add damage and later strip enemy stat buffs. Personal shields and rising Haste help him survive long enough to cycle that payoff. Without varied stat-reduction support, the rolls remain unreliable and his damage ceiling falls sharply.",
  "counter_overview": "In PVP, [[Eryndor]] uses a **high-energy ultimate** to roll all enemies; stat reductions from different allies add Woe stacks that make each later roll more punishing. Pressure [[Eryndor]] and those debuff providers before the stacks make his stat theft reliable; changing your own damage type does not stop enemy-side stacking. His low Magic DEF makes early rear pressure with [[filter:magic-backline-assassin]] like [[Evie]] or [[Nerion]] effective. Use [[Lily May]] to cancel Forced Game if the interrupt window is available, and race the first cast with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
}